<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Bass units shares move on merge talk.</title>
<headline>Czech Bass units shares move on merge talk.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Czech brewers Radegast and Prague Breweries, 33 percent and 51 percent respectively owned by Bass Plc, moved sharply on Thursday after Bass said it was considering merger prospects for the two breweries.</p>
<p>Radegast rose 252 crowns, 4.9 percent, to 5,307 while Prague Breweries lost, 4.9 percent, 120 crowns, to 2,282. Most shares on the Prague bourse, including the above two breweries, can move up or down by a maximum of five percent during each session.</p>
</text>
